= Collective action — Simple =

Collective action occurs when an outcome depends on what many participants do. A group may all benefit if enough people contribute, yet each person can sometimes benefit by letting others bear the cost. Institutions and norms can change those incentives.

'''Important boundary:''' collective action ≠ coordination problem.

